-- title:
--   Hurewicz map is injective on a reduced CW model ((r+1)-cell relations)
-- statement:
--   The Hurewicz map is injective: $(r+1)$-cells give the same relations.
--
--   Let $r=n+2$ and let $Y$ be a reduced CW model in degree $r$ with $H_i(Y;\mathbb{Z})=0$ for all $0<i<r$.  Then the Hurewicz homomorphism $h:\pi_r(Y,y)\to H_r(Y;\mathbb{Z})$ is injective.
--
--   The kernel of $h$ is generated by the attaching maps of the $(r+1)$-cells of $Y$: an element of $\pi_r$ dies in homology precisely when it bounds such a cell.  These are exactly the relations $\partial C_{r+1}$ that cut out $H_r=C_r/\partial C_{r+1}$.  Because the low homotopy and low homology of $Y$ both vanish, the two descriptions of the quotient agree and $\ker h=0$.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The statement takes the Hurewicz map $h$ as an explicit additive homomorphism argument and concludes `Function.Injective h`, the complementary half to the surjectivity child.
-- source:
--   A. Hatcher, Algebraic Topology, Cambridge University Press (2002), §4.2 Theorem 4.32 (Hurewicz) p. 366 and Proposition 4.13 (cellular approximation) p. 353; and https://zhuanlan.zhihu.com/p/2063085365225863035 (the three-step proof sketch followed here).

import Mathlib.Topology.Homotopy.HomotopyGroup
import Mathlib.Topology.Category.TopCat.Basic
import Definitions.Def_HurewiczSketchV2
import Definitions.Def_SP4Homology

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace HurewiczSketchV2

/-- The Hurewicz map is injective: `(r+1)`-cells give the same relations.

Let `r = n+2` and let `Y` be a reduced CW model in degree `r` whose homology vanishes
in degrees `0 < i < r`.  Then the Hurewicz homomorphism
`h : π_r(Y,y) → H_r(Y;ℤ)` is injective.

This is the "relations" half of the cellular comparison in the Hurewicz proof.  The
kernel of `π_r → H_r` is generated by the attaching maps of the `(r+1)`-cells, and
these impose exactly the same relations on the cellular chain group `C_r` that define
`H_r = C_r / ∂C_{r+1}`.  Since the low homotopy and low homology both vanish, the two
quotients coincide and `h` has trivial kernel. -/
theorem hurewicz_injective_of_reduced_cw (n : ℕ) (Y : TopCat) (y : Y)
    (hY : ReducedCWModel (n + 2) Y)
    (hH : ∀ i : ℕ, 0 < i → i < n + 2 → CategoryTheory.Limits.IsZero (SP4Homology.H i Y))
    (h : Additive (HomotopyGroup.Pi (n + 2) Y y) →+ SP4Homology.H (n + 2) Y) :
    Function.Injective h := by
  sorry

end HurewiczSketchV2
